id: hac-3kz8
title: Implement typed repairs and related-resource command contracts
description: "Build fully typed Home Assistant Repairs WebSocket/REST flow support and bounded search/related resource topology commands with strict validation, safe writes, stable formats, docs, tests, setup proof, and release-safe delivery."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,implementation,repairs,search,typescript,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-05T19:18:16.357Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T20:09:07.750Z"
deadline: "2026-08-07T19:18:16.357Z"
assignee: codex-root
claim_principal: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Repairs commands cover list, get-issue-data, ignore/unignore, and fix-flow start/get/submit with typed request/response contracts and read-only enforcement; Related command validates all Core 2026.8 item types, supports count and positive safe-integer per-type limits, sorts deterministic resource arrays, and reports upstream failures honestly; CLI registration, exports, schema/help E2E, README, docs/API, docs/INDEX, docs/LLM_INTEGRATION, and docs/AGENT_OPTIMIZATION are current and linked; Focused, full, exact coverage, docstring, type, lint, duplication, file-size, ShellCheck, PM, changelog, audit, Trivy, history-secret, package, wizard/settings, live all-format, and auto-release dry-run gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "Feature and plan capture complete duplicate-safe lineage, research, privacy, safety, and release constraints"
goal: complete-agent-home-assistant-interface
objective: implement-repairs-topology-contracts
value: Replace raw protocol construction with predictable typed commands optimized for agents and CI.
impact: Makes Home Assistant configuration health and resource dependencies actionable without sacrificing safety or format stability.
outcome: "Reviewed source, tests, docs, and live structural evidence merged on master."
why_now: These built-in Core contracts are stable and live but absent from the first-class hassio command surface.
parent: hac-ha2t
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: api-parity-2026-08
release: unreleased
